WEBVTT

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:10.820
So Ra No Wo To

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:49.720
Man, I hate this stupid snow!

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:54.320
Especially now that HQ's said we need
to be sure to do all our patrols.

00:01:56.590 --> 00:02:00.930
You still haven't given up over
Jacott-san, have you?

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:03.080
That's not exactly it.

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:05.120
Well, I don't think there's
anything wrong with it.

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:06.640
You can look all you want,

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:10.980
and if you don't find anyone,
you can still believe they're alive.

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:15.400
What?

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:20.570
Kureha-chan, I thought you might be looking
like Rio-sempai for a second there.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:32.850
What's wrong?

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:34.030
Under that cliff!

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:35.900
Eleven o'clock!

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:37.670
Four hundred meters or so out!

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:55.190
Wake up!

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:56.850
Hey, wake up!

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:02.500
Even his clothes are frozen!

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:04.710
Kanata, take off his coat.

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:07.030
We'll change coats with him.

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:08.080
OK!

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:10.960
Look at him...

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:15.460
A Roman soldier!

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:24.410
A Visitor - A Burning Field of Snow

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:41.740
I can't believe you were actually able
to bring back this facility.

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:45.750
I can see how you earned your reputation
as the greatest genius in academy history.

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:48.790
Now victory is ours!

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:52.540
It's all thanks to you,
Kannagi Noël-kun.

00:03:58.220 --> 00:03:59.710
Noël-chan!

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:06.890
While on patrol, the two
of them found her.

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:08.850
It's a Roman soldier.

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:12.160
Her left leg is broken.

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:19.120
Her fingers are turning
black and red!

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:25.790
Frostbite. If we're not careful,
she'll lose the fingers.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:33.540
The witch of Helvetia...

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:39.880
Leave her to me!

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:51.380
Looks like she'll be fine.

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:53.290
The fingers are OK, too.

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:54.730
Great!

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:56.230
Where's Noël-chan?

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:58.990
She said she'd stay with
her for a while.

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:03.990
But I don't know... She seemed to think
this was really important,

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:07.110
like when she was fixing
the Takemikazuchi.

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:08.990
I see...

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:16.290
A trumpet.

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:20.590
She might be a spy, yeah...

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:23.590
I was really surprised.

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:25.220
Well, yeah.

00:05:26.230 --> 00:05:29.660
No one thought we'd run into
a Roman soldier there.

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:34.260
No. It was the first time I've ever
seen anyone from Rome.

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:36.850
They say they're all
enemies, right?

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:42.420
So I was thinking they'd
be scarier somehow.

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:46.740
The people of Rome probably
think the same about us.

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:52.780
But I realized, when I saw her...

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:55.120
They're just like us.

00:05:56.470 --> 00:05:58.030
Hey, Kanata, you...

00:05:58.030 --> 00:05:58.870
Hey, Kana-chan.

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:02.250
It's almost time for school
lessons to end.

00:06:09.790 --> 00:06:13.560
The peace talks are still
going badly, aren't they?

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:15.350
So I hear.

00:06:16.530 --> 00:06:19.010
Are we reporting her?

00:06:19.010 --> 00:06:24.580
If we do, she'll be taken to the
Capitol and interrogated.

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:29.020
We have to!

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:33.640
They're invading enemy territory
during unstable times!

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:35.180
A soldier should be prepared
for torture...

00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:36.040
Interrogation.

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:43.460
I will decide what to do with her.

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:48.300
Please give me some
time, Kureha-chan.

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:53.300
Don't forget, Captain.

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:57.160
We're soldiers.

00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:07.260
Can I ask one thing?

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:11.270
Did you meet anyone when you
were carrying her here?

00:07:13.230 --> 00:07:16.200
I don't know.

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:18.030
OK.

00:07:18.030 --> 00:07:19.200
Thanks.

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:42.040
Say, Rio. What would you do?

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:26.020
A Helvetian soldier...

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:37.660
What were you going
to do with these?

00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:48.090
Where am I?

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:50.300
Am I a Helvetian prisoner?

00:08:52.810 --> 00:08:54.980
I don't speak Roman.

00:08:54.980 --> 00:08:55.820
Fine.

00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:57.300
So you took me prisoner-

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:02.180
What was that scream?

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:03.540
What's wrong?

00:09:05.470 --> 00:09:07.610
She woke up.

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:10.360
I'm glad.

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:23.620
Imperial Roman Army, First Armored
Division, 13th Legion B-Company

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:29.710
Master Sergeant Aisha Aldola,
serial number 1031021.

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:32.290
What are you doing here?

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:36.340
Imperial Roman Army, Warrant Officer
Aisha Aldola, serial number 1031021.

00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:37.970
What was your mission?

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:42.270
<Identification number 1031021.>

00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:46.690
You've got guts, then.

00:09:48.830 --> 00:09:51.070
Well? Did you learn anything?

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:52.570
Not a thing!

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:55.880
She doesn't speak any Helvetian.

00:09:55.880 --> 00:10:00.500
All we learned was her serial number
and that her name is Aisha.

00:10:01.990 --> 00:10:04.520
I'm Lieutenant Filicia Heidemann.

00:10:04.520 --> 00:10:06.520
I'm in charge of this fortress.

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:13.090
You have really nice breasts,
just the kind I like.

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:17.060
Would it be all right if I played
with them for a bit?

00:10:17.060 --> 00:10:19.590
Can I run my fingers
all along your body?

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:25.830
What are you saying, Captain?

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:30.350
She really seems unable to
understand Helvetian.

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:35.360
But this is a problem. We can't
interrogate her like this.

00:10:36.100 --> 00:10:39.860
We need to find someone
who speaks Roman.

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:41.920
Then...

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:45.950
Until we can interrogate her
and file a proper report,

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:48.460
we'll keep her here.

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:49.810
But...

00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:53.880
I thought I'd place a bet.

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:57.510
I've got no part in this.

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:03.130
Aisha-chan, welcome to
Clocktower Fortress.

00:11:03.130 --> 00:11:05.420
<Clocktower Fortress?>

00:11:05.420 --> 00:11:07.770
Yup, Clocktower Fortress.

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:11.770
<Ah, I see... Then I made it.>

00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:14.780
<Grandmother...>

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:35.600
Maybe it's too hot.

00:11:54.170 --> 00:11:55.110
She ate it.

00:11:56.170 --> 00:11:57.400
Is it good?

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:01.400
<To escape, I need stamina,
so I'll eat your food.>

00:12:02.270 --> 00:12:04.590
I'm sure she's saying it's good!

00:12:06.680 --> 00:12:08.180
What's going on here?

00:12:08.180 --> 00:12:10.280
Kanata's always like this,

00:12:10.280 --> 00:12:12.580
but Noël's never that
nice to anyone...

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:16.090
She may be trying to atone.

00:12:18.980 --> 00:12:23.090
Have you ever seen
a fossil of an angel?

00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:25.450
Angel?

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:32.540
<They don't understand me, I know...
What's wrong with me?>

00:12:32.540 --> 00:12:35.660
I should have studied Roman.

00:12:35.660 --> 00:12:36.950
That's right.

00:12:36.950 --> 00:12:39.170
If we could talk, we could...

00:12:42.820 --> 00:12:44.820
Working hard, huh?

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:46.320
Hey, Yumina-chan?

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:49.300
You guys got enough people at
the church to help shovel?

00:12:49.300 --> 00:12:50.610
Yes.

00:12:50.610 --> 00:12:53.400
The kids are really working at it.

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:54.830
Glad to hear it.

00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:58.340
I guess they're really growing up.

00:12:59.070 --> 00:13:00.280
That's right.

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:05.710
People grow and get
better every day.

00:13:05.710 --> 00:13:08.190
Just like Kanata-san's
trumpet playing...

00:13:08.740 --> 00:13:12.040
Rio would say she's not there yet.

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:16.580
Hey, weren't you heading to
Treize to buy more goods?

00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:20.010
Some stuff happened, and I ended up
having to come back.

00:13:20.470 --> 00:13:22.810
Sorry to hear that.

00:13:23.130 --> 00:13:25.860
Oh, speaking of the Fortress,

00:13:26.230 --> 00:13:29.370
I heard this awful rumor...

00:13:32.150 --> 00:13:34.030
Thank you!

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:35.830
<It's a wonderful melody.>

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:40.450
<Ah, I didn't know there were
trumpets like that left.>

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:44.590
<Can I play it?>

00:13:46.030 --> 00:13:48.840
I think Rio-sempai would let you.

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:10.870
<It's a good trumpet.>

00:14:11.150 --> 00:14:12.750
<Really, I haven't seen
one this nice...>

00:14:12.050 --> 00:14:13.620
That song was amazing!

00:14:13.920 --> 00:14:16.870
This is so wonderful!

00:14:17.270 --> 00:14:28.270
Iliya's song filled me up, and then Rio-sempai's,
and the same song is in Roman, too!

00:14:30.130 --> 00:14:32.140
Sound really does fill the air!

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:36.370
The same way in Rome
and in Helvetia.

00:14:50.150 --> 00:14:51.740
First aid.

00:15:02.690 --> 00:15:04.330
<Danke.>

00:15:04.330 --> 00:15:05.480
Dan...ke?

00:15:05.480 --> 00:15:07.410
<Yeah, danke.>

00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:09.780
What's "danke"?

00:15:09.780 --> 00:15:11.510
It means "Thank you."

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:17.490
I thought someone saw us.

00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:22.090
This city never bore the
full brunt of the war,

00:15:22.090 --> 00:15:30.280
but almost everyone here's lost family and
friends, one way or another, in the war.

00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:34.580
They're nice people,
but you know...

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:36.550
Mikhail,

00:15:36.550 --> 00:15:40.060
you remember the guy who
runs that distillery?

00:15:41.880 --> 00:15:45.390
I was at his place until yesterday.

00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:50.170
He said the Helvetian
Army's on the move,

00:15:50.910 --> 00:15:52.960
heading here.

00:15:54.440 --> 00:15:59.210
If that's got something to do with a Roman
scout being all the way out here,

00:15:59.210 --> 00:16:00.720
then it's a big deal.

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:07.000
Anyway, we need to ask her.

00:16:07.460 --> 00:16:12.300
Naomi-san, do you know anyone
who speaks Roman?

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:15.400
I sure do!

00:16:21.590 --> 00:16:23.170
I am Yumina.

00:16:24.270 --> 00:16:27.600
I am a servant of the Helvetian
Orthodox Church.

00:16:27.600 --> 00:16:30.460
May the blessings of
the all be upon you.

00:16:31.410 --> 00:16:32.390
Heretic.

00:16:32.390 --> 00:16:33.840
There's one God.

00:16:34.520 --> 00:16:38.350
That greeting is blasphemy.

00:16:38.670 --> 00:16:40.310
What are you saying to her?

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:42.490
Just a greeting.

00:16:42.490 --> 00:16:45.260
Go on! Ask her!

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:47.530
Why are you here?

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:55.050
If you don't tell us, you put everyone
here in a very bad position.

00:16:56.290 --> 00:17:02.000
If you feel any sort of obligation to them,
then tell us the truth.

00:17:10.910 --> 00:17:14.510
I can't tell you about my mission.

00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:19.140
But I wanted to see the
Angel Fossil located in this town.

00:17:20.620 --> 00:17:23.730
She says she wants to
see the Angel Fossil.

00:17:23.870 --> 00:17:25.530
Angel Fossil...

00:17:25.530 --> 00:17:26.730
What?

00:17:29.580 --> 00:17:34.790
My grandmother was
a Maiden here.

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:38.490
My grandmother was
a soldier here.

00:17:38.490 --> 00:17:41.620
<She was captured at the Eastern Front
and met my grandfather.>

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:45.050
She was captured at the Eastern Front
and met my grandfather.

00:17:45.050 --> 00:17:47.970
<As I grew up, I listened
to her stories.>

00:17:47.970 --> 00:17:50.500
I grew up listening to her stories.

00:17:52.360 --> 00:17:57.550
<So I wanted to see the Angel of the apocalypse
that brought judgment

00:17:57.550 --> 00:18:02.590
to the world in the distant past,
the one my grandmother spoke of.>

00:18:03.460 --> 00:18:05.510
That doctrine is wrong!

00:18:05.510 --> 00:18:07.900
It was the devil that destroyed
the world!

00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:11.110
Just tell us exactly
what she said!

00:18:13.840 --> 00:18:17.950
She wanted to see the angel of the apocalypse
that destroyed the world.

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:20.550
That's why she came...

00:18:22.710 --> 00:18:24.370
A call to advance?

00:18:24.850 --> 00:18:26.580
That code is...

00:18:29.490 --> 00:18:33.850
Royal Guard Platoon, 9th Independent
Mobile Division...

00:18:33.850 --> 00:18:36.060
The 9th... It can't be...

00:18:36.060 --> 00:18:37.590
Colonel Hopkins!

00:18:38.230 --> 00:18:40.010
Is he famous?

00:18:40.320 --> 00:18:43.360
He's known as the
Demon of Vingt.

00:18:43.360 --> 00:18:46.060
They say he brought weapons
back from the old age,

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:49.740
wiping out three towns
in a single night.

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:57.500
It's all right. He doesn't
know you're here.

00:18:57.500 --> 00:18:59.020
It's all right.

00:18:59.020 --> 00:19:03.010
Either way, you don't have
time to worry about it.

00:19:03.010 --> 00:19:07.130
You need to decide what you're
going to do, and fast.

00:19:07.130 --> 00:19:08.320
You can either give her over...

00:19:08.320 --> 00:19:10.250
There's nothing to decide!

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:13.410
We're Helvetian Soldiers!

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:16.330
I lost the bet.

00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:19.340
You didn't make it in
time, did you, Rio?

00:19:19.340 --> 00:19:20.760
Wait!

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:25.350
Rio didn't want anyone
else to suffer.

00:19:25.350 --> 00:19:28.020
That's why she'd do what
she could, she said!

00:19:28.410 --> 00:19:30.850
That's why she left, wasn't it?

00:19:31.670 --> 00:19:35.030
I don't want this to happen!

00:19:35.980 --> 00:19:37.530
We're all the same!

00:19:37.880 --> 00:19:39.680
We're all together!

00:19:40.210 --> 00:19:45.160
I will now give my order as leader
of the 1121st Platoon.

00:19:46.570 --> 00:19:54.130
This order is mine alone, and I will
take full responsibility for it.

00:19:54.910 --> 00:19:56.920
Are we clear, everyone?

00:20:06.220 --> 00:20:11.190
I am Commander of the 1121st Platoon,
Lieutenant Filicia Heidemann.

00:20:11.190 --> 00:20:15.110
Yesterday, a Roman scout
was captured in Treize.

00:20:16.240 --> 00:20:21.860
Unfortunately, there was an accident during
questioning, and we didn't get any details.

00:20:21.860 --> 00:20:27.780
We've actually had reports of
a Roman soldier here in Seize.

00:20:28.230 --> 00:20:29.870
Do you have any ideas?

00:20:30.330 --> 00:20:32.370
No, Colonel.

00:20:33.030 --> 00:20:34.500
Understood.

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:39.260
As of this moment,
the 1121st Fortress

00:20:39.260 --> 00:20:42.650
is under the command of the 9th
Independent Mobile Division.

00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:54.030
Stay quiet.

00:20:54.030 --> 00:20:55.670
I'm sorry.

00:20:55.670 --> 00:21:00.400
Aisha was telling me about the
legend of the Flame Maidens.

00:21:00.900 --> 00:21:02.320
But it's strange...

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:03.210
According to her...

00:21:03.210 --> 00:21:04.460
Shh!

00:21:05.470 --> 00:21:06.950
Search everywhere!

00:21:06.950 --> 00:21:08.270
Did you find her?

00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:10.010
What about over there?

00:21:10.010 --> 00:21:11.130
Nothing over here!

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:12.210
Find her!

00:21:12.210 --> 00:21:13.790
Open this door!

00:21:14.610 --> 00:21:16.040
She's gotta be here somewhere!

00:21:16.040 --> 00:21:18.010
Post more guards by the exits!

00:21:27.040 --> 00:21:30.520
I hadn't asked your name
yet, she says.

00:21:30.520 --> 00:21:31.180
Noël...

00:21:31.580 --> 00:21:33.390
Ihr name ist Noël.

00:21:34.290 --> 00:21:37.350
Noël... Noël Kannagi?

00:21:37.640 --> 00:21:38.570
Ja...

00:21:39.130 --> 00:21:40.610
The Witch of Helvetia...

00:21:40.610 --> 00:21:42.180
The Invisible Reaper...

00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:45.240
The Invisible Reaper?

00:21:55.910 --> 00:21:56.870
A rat, maybe?

00:21:57.840 --> 00:21:58.710
Noël-san?

00:22:13.400 --> 00:22:15.290
Hello?

00:22:15.290 --> 00:22:17.390
This is the 1121st Fortress.

00:22:20.750 --> 00:22:25.570
A massive Roman Army contingent has appeared
at the Seize border with No Man's Land?

00:24:15.010 --> 00:24:19.930
Fill the Blue Sky

00:24:16.390 --> 00:24:17.070
Next time:

00:24:17.070 --> 00:24:19.270
Fill the Blue Sky.

00:24:19.930 --> 00:24:25.010
This program is a work of fiction.
Any resemblance to people, parties,
or situations is purely coincidental.
